# Dependencies — each package installs its own.
node_modules/

# Build output / caches
.next/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. Real keys live in ~/.devdigest/secrets.json (mode 0600), never here.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Cloned user repos — see AGENTS.md "Do not touch".
server/clones/

# The design bundle and everything unpacked from it. The .html is 1.7 MB of
# base64+gzip assets behind a JSON manifest (INSIGHTS.md, "Tool & Library
# Notes") — it does not diff, and committing it would weigh the history down
# forever. Keep it locally; regenerate design-mocks/ from it rather than commit.
DevDigest Design (standalone).html
design-mocks/

# Failure screenshots written by the e2e runner. e2e/README.md has always
# described these as git-ignored; they never actually were.
e2e/test-results/

# Local agent/session state. `.claude/skills/` and `.claude/agents/` are shared:
# AGENTS.md tells every agent to run `engineering-insights`, so the skill has to
# travel with the repo, and the agent set encodes this repo's own gates, layering
# rules and doc surfaces — it is worth no more than the repo it was written for.
#
# `.claude/hooks/` and `.claude/settings.json` are shared for the same reason:
# `specreator` is fenced to `specs/` by a PreToolUse hook, not by its prompt, so
# an agent set that travels without the hook that bounds it is a set whose stated
# guarantees are false. `settings.local.json` stays personal and stays ignored.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# Failure screenshots from the browser suite — regenerated per run, never committed
# (e2e/README.md has always claimed these were ignored; they were not).
e2e/test-results/
